# Code owners. Branch rules require a code owner's approving review for a pull request that touches
# any path below (ADR-0023, ADR-0029). Everything else merges on the factory's checks:
# tier low and medium automatically, tier high after `factory/human-approval`.
#
# Replace @yaf/maintainers with the real team. The team must contain humans only: no app, no bot,
# no machine user. An approving review is the one thing an agent cannot produce.
#
# Keep this list in step with `sensitivePaths` in .github/factory/policy.json. The policy is wider on
# purpose: it also makes paths tier high that need a human review without needing a code OWNER
# (Directory.Packages.props and .editorconfig: a change the plan declared is tier medium, a patch update to
# Directory.Packages.props must be able to merge automatically, and any other change to either is tier high; ADR-0034).

# What is to be built, and the decisions
/specs/**/spec.md                          @yaf/maintainers
/specs/0000-framework/                     @yaf/maintainers
/adr/                                      @yaf/maintainers

# The factory itself, CI and agent instructions
/.github/                                  @yaf/maintainers
/.claude/                                  @yaf/maintainers
/.agents/                                  @yaf/maintainers
AGENTS.md                                  @yaf/maintainers
/CLAUDE.md                                 @yaf/maintainers

# Guards
